# chora_test's manifest (#963).
#
# It holds nothing itself: it finds the network card through the HAL, asks
# the kernel whether the card is claimed, and starts chora on it twice -- and
# once on QEMU's educational device, where the board has one (#977).
#
# 🔑 What it MAY HAND ON is the whole of it.  A chora it starts asks for a
# capability for its one function (#964), and exec_load() cuts that to this
# line (#743): any function, since a manifest names no address (#982), with
# DMA, registers and the interrupt.  So the second chora on the card is
# refused by the claim the first holds, not by a capability it lacks.

name chora_test
delegatable 12 any 0x7
